{"schema":"SDW_SCRIPTURE_CHAPTER_V1","revision":"52add6f41edc5dd9c21f65f02f933fbd1cec266285bee8bce249607475050398","canonicalSourceHash":"f9dfbce6dd2edfe4bb3b4690acd6622f392035be2b0349df98f3607f0a05f6c2","bookId":"engwebu:job","chapter":41,"verses":[{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":41,"verse_ordinal":1020,"verse_start":1,"verse_end":1,"verse_label":"1","text":"“Can you draw out Leviathan with a fish hook, or press down his tongue with a cord?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3266},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":41,"verse_ordinal":1021,"verse_start":2,"verse_end":2,"verse_label":"2","text":"Can you put a rope into his nose, or pierce his jaw through with a hook?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3269},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":41,"verse_ordinal":1022,"verse_start":3,"verse_end":3,"verse_label":"3","text":"Will he make many petitions to you, or will he speak soft words to you?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3272},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":41,"verse_ordinal":1023,"verse_start":4,"verse_end":4,"verse_label":"4","text":"Will he make a covenant with you, that you should take him for a servant forever?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3275},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":41,"verse_ordinal":1024,"verse_start":5,"verse_end":5,"verse_label":"5","text":"Will you play with him as with a bird? Or will you bind him for your girls?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3278},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":41,"verse_ordinal":1025,"verse_start":6,"verse_end":6,"verse_label":"6","text":"Will traders barter for him? Will they part him among the merchants?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3281},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":41,"verse_ordinal":1026,"verse_start":7,"verse_end":7,"verse_label":"7","text":"Can you fill his skin with barbed irons, or his head with fish spears?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3284},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":41,"verse_ordinal":1027,"verse_start":8,"verse_end":8,"verse_label":"8","text":"Lay your hand on him. Remember the battle, and do so no more.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3287},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":41,"verse_ordinal":1028,"verse_start":9,"verse_end":9,"verse_label":"9","text":"Behold, the hope of him is in vain. Won’t one be cast down even at the sight of him?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3290},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":41,"verse_ordinal":1029,"verse_start":10,"verse_end":10,"verse_label":"10","text":"None is so fierce that he dare stir him up. Who then is he who can stand before me?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3294},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":41,"verse_ordinal":1030,"verse_start":11,"verse_end":11,"verse_label":"11","text":"Who has first given to me, that I should repay him? Everything under the heavens is mine.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3297},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":41,"verse_ordinal":1031,"verse_start":12,"verse_end":12,"verse_label":"12","text":"“I will not keep silence concerning his limbs, nor his mighty strength, nor his goodly frame.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3301},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":41,"verse_ordinal":1032,"verse_start":13,"verse_end":13,"verse_label":"13","text":"Who can strip off his outer garment? Who will come within his jaws?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3304},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":41,"verse_ordinal":1033,"verse_start":14,"verse_end":14,"verse_label":"14","text":"Who can open the doors of his face? Around his teeth is terror.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3307},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":41,"verse_ordinal":1034,"verse_start":15,"verse_end":15,"verse_label":"15","text":"Strong scales are his pride, shut up together with a close seal.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3310},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":41,"verse_ordinal":1035,"verse_start":16,"verse_end":16,"verse_label":"16","text":"One is so near to another, that no air can come between them.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3314},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":41,"verse_ordinal":1036,"verse_start":17,"verse_end":17,"verse_label":"17","text":"They are joined to one another. They stick together, so that they can’t be pulled apart.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3317},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":41,"verse_ordinal":1037,"verse_start":18,"verse_end":18,"verse_label":"18","text":"His sneezing flashes out light. His eyes are like the eyelids of the morning.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3320},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":41,"verse_ordinal":1038,"verse_start":19,"verse_end":19,"verse_label":"19","text":"Out of his mouth go burning torches. Sparks of fire leap out.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3323},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":41,"verse_ordinal":1039,"verse_start":20,"verse_end":20,"verse_label":"20","text":"Out of his nostrils a smoke goes, as of a boiling pot over a fire of reeds.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3326},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":41,"verse_ordinal":1040,"verse_start":21,"verse_end":21,"verse_label":"21","text":"His breath kindles coals. A flame goes out of his mouth.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3329},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":41,"verse_ordinal":1041,"verse_start":22,"verse_end":22,"verse_label":"22","text":"There is strength in his neck. Terror dances before him.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3332},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":41,"verse_ordinal":1042,"verse_start":23,"verse_end":23,"verse_label":"23","text":"The flakes of his flesh are joined together. They are firm on him. They can’t be moved.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3335},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":41,"verse_ordinal":1043,"verse_start":24,"verse_end":24,"verse_label":"24","text":"His heart is as firm as a stone, yes, firm as the lower millstone.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3339},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":41,"verse_ordinal":1044,"verse_start":25,"verse_end":25,"verse_label":"25","text":"When he raises himself up, the mighty are afraid. They retreat before his thrashing.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3342},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":41,"verse_ordinal":1045,"verse_start":26,"verse_end":26,"verse_label":"26","text":"If one attacks him with the sword, it can’t prevail; nor the spear, the dart, nor the pointed shaft.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3345},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":41,"verse_ordinal":1046,"verse_start":27,"verse_end":27,"verse_label":"27","text":"He counts iron as straw, and bronze as rotten wood.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3348},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":41,"verse_ordinal":1047,"verse_start":28,"verse_end":28,"verse_label":"28","text":"The arrow can’t make him flee. Sling stones are like chaff to him.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3351},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":41,"verse_ordinal":1048,"verse_start":29,"verse_end":29,"verse_label":"29","text":"Clubs are counted as stubble. He laughs at the rushing of the javelin.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3354},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":41,"verse_ordinal":1049,"verse_start":30,"verse_end":30,"verse_label":"30","text":"His undersides are like sharp potsherds, leaving a trail in the mud like a threshing sledge.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3357},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":41,"verse_ordinal":1050,"verse_start":31,"verse_end":31,"verse_label":"31","text":"He makes the deep to boil like a pot. He makes the sea like a pot of ointment.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3360},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":41,"verse_ordinal":1051,"verse_start":32,"verse_end":32,"verse_label":"32","text":"He makes a path shine after him. One would think the deep had white hair.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3363},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":41,"verse_ordinal":1052,"verse_start":33,"verse_end":33,"verse_label":"33","text":"On earth there is not his equal, that is made without fear.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3366},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":41,"verse_ordinal":1053,"verse_start":34,"verse_end":34,"verse_label":"34","text":"He sees everything that is high. He is king over all the sons of pride.”","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3369}]}